<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tianshui</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tianshui is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a>. It lies close to the region where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> had its origins, and was later a frontier prefecture on the roads to the west, briefly the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> state in 617–618. Nearby are the Buddhist grottoes of Maijishan, carved from about the 5th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tianshui.jpg" alt="Tianshui" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: shizhao · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%BC%8F%E7%BE%B2%E5%BA%99%E7%89%8C%E5%9D%8A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
